---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import OpensInNewTab from '../components/OpensInNewTab.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="bulsu.tools is an independent, student-led open-source collective that makes free campus utilities for Bulacan State University."
>
 <Header />
 <main id="main-content" class="legal-main">
 <div class="container legal-container">
 <a href="/" class="legal-back">&larr; Home</a>

 <header class="legal-hero">
 <h1>About bulsu.tools</h1>
 <p class="legal-lede">
 <strong>bulsu.tools</strong> is an independent, student-led open-source
 collective at Bulacan State University. We're
 <strong>not</strong> officially affiliated with, endorsed by or
 representing the BulSU administration.
 </p>
 </header>

 <article class="legal-body">
 <section>
 <h2>Who we are</h2>
 <p>
 We are BulSU students who build free campus utilities in our
 spare time. The project started with Geary, a student-managed handbook
 of enrollment, academics and campus guides, plus a fork of the UPLB
 Room TBA campus map adapted for Malolos. It grew into a small collective
 that maintains several tools and mentors new contributors along the way.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>What we build</h2>
 <ul>
 <li>
 Geary is a static handbook of student guides for BulSU, each article
 citing its official source.
 </li>
 <li>
 The GWA Calculator computes General Weighted Averages and estimates
 eligibility for the Gold Gear Awards and Latin Honors, entirely in the
 browser.
 </li>
 <li>
 Room TBA is an interactive map of the Malolos Campus 1 and Campus 2
 buildings, forked from the UPLB campus map.
 </li>
 </ul>
 <p>
 Everything is open source under MIT on{" "}
 <a href="https://github.com/bulsutools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub<OpensInNewTab /></a>.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>How we work</h2>
 <p>
 bulsu.tools doubles as a training ground. Contributors learn real
 software engineering through pull requests, peer code review, and
 release cycles. If you're a student who wants to ship something people
 use, this is a good place to start.
 </p>
 </section>

 <section>
 <h2>Contact</h2>
 <p>
 Open an issue or discussion on{" "}
 <a href="https://github.com/bulsutools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub<OpensInNewTab /></a>.
 </p>
 </section>
 </article>
 </div>
 </main>
 <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
.legal-main {
 min-height: 100vh;
 padding-top: 4rem;
 padding-bottom: 2rem;
 border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
 }

.legal-container {
 max-width: 44rem;
 }

.legal-back {
 font-size: 0.85rem;
 color: var(--text-muted);
 text-decoration: none;
 display: inline-block;
 margin-bottom: 2rem;
 }

.legal-back:hover {
 color: var(--brand-maroon);
 }


.legal-hero h1 {
 font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
 margin: 0 0 1rem;
 }

.legal-lede {
 margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
 font-size: 0.95rem;
 }

.legal-body section {
 margin-bottom: 2rem;
 }

.legal-body h2 {
 font-size: 1.15rem;
 margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
 }

.legal-body ul {
 margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
 padding-left: 1.25rem;
 }

.legal-body li {
 margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
 }

.legal-body a {
 color: var(--brand-maroon);
 text-decoration: underline;
 text-underline-offset: 2px;
 }

.legal-body a:hover {
 color: var(--brand-maroon-deep);
 }
</style>
